## VM args for CI/test BEAM nodes, applied via
## `erl -args_file config/vm.args.test' by the eunit launcher
## (scripts/github_workflow.sh), the e2e launcher (bin/e2e_ct), and the
## peer BEAMs they spawn (apps/arweave/test/ar_test_node.erl).
##
## Policy: test nodes share a CI runner with the GitHub Actions agent, so
## idle schedulers must SLEEP, not busy-wait/spin. Spinning saturates the
## box and starves the agent's heartbeat -> GitHub kills the job as "the
## self-hosted runner lost communication with the server". (Production,
## config/vm.args.src, sets these to `very_long' for the opposite reason:
## a dedicated miner that owns its box and wants latency over politeness.)
##
## `+S' (scheduler count) is intentionally NOT set here: it is
## workload-specific and set inline per launcher -- eunit pins `+S 4:4',
## e2e is tunable via AR_E2E_SCHEDULERS (default 8); peer BEAMs inherit
## the coordinator's value via erlang:system_info(schedulers_online).
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
